### Summary

Reviewed the 8 files of part 1. No blocker or fix. The group-move busy lock now flows through activeTransactionDeps to both the switch and relocate paths, which is correct (index.ts:346-347, 363, 480; relocate.ts:24-25, 33). Findings are two docs items and one test gap, all "consider": the backlog doc (line 26) and the spec relocate row (line 1302) still say relocate is refused only while a recording or export runs, and the dialog test's refusal list has no "moving" case. Four open review threads on these files are addressed in the current code. Two open contracts remain: whether a switch can overlap the start of a move (gate.ts not read), and whether the renderer clears the lock from the list broadcast (renderer consumer not read). For the spec, I read the IPC table region in full and grepped the rest for the relocate wording, not the whole 1,300-line file.

